  "story": {
    "day": 81,
    "title": "Kaya's Winter Break",
    "sentences": [
      "On Saturday, December tenth, two thousand twenty-two, Kaya turned fourteen.",
      "She was excited to spend her autumn break learning about Bali island, Indonesia.",
      "First, one hundred other children learned about Hindu gods and customs on computer.",
      "Wow, most people dreamed to touch a white beach or Mt. Agung, a mountain.",
      "Their fifth gift was hers: a guitar. Two other friends brought an egg tart.",
      "A jogging suit was on sale at a store for fifty dollars; it was a good deal.",
      "Kaya had healthy Chinese fish and seaweed with iced tea to drink.",
      "Usually, she took a shower before bed. A child drew with chalk near their house.",
      "Eighty ninety other people saw nine Chinese lanterns. Thirty of them were lit.",
      "The twelfth day, Kaya studied different subjects in her dictionary, which was useful.",
      "Forty minutes later, her boss spoke about a captain's third interview.",
      "The second subject was fun. Her fourth gift was one mile of books. Theirs was a good deal."
    ]
  }
}